1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Part 2. You will hear a short talk given to a group of retired people about a club called Connect.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
First you have some time to look at questions 11 to 15.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 15.

4
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Hello, I've been asked to talk to you today about Connect. Connect is a club for people who have retired from full-time work.

5
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The first Connect club began back in 1960 in Brisbane, Australia.

6
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Today I'll concentrate on Frankston Connect, the club where I'm a member. It services the communities around the suburb of Frankston here in Melbourne.

7
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Okay, so what are our club aims? We're not a fitness club or anything like that. Some Connect branches do charity work, but that's not for us.

8
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Our objective is to provide social contact with others who have similar interests and ideas.

9
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Now meetings, we have monthly club meetings where the usual club business is discussed.

10
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
For example, at the last meeting we talked about how much money was spent that month.

11
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Also at that meeting someone had just returned from an overseas trip and he spoke about that.

12
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Then we looked at entries for our photography competition. The winner will be announced soon.

13
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Up until now we've used the school hall for our meetings, but that's about to be renovated so we needed to find an alternative.

14
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:22,000
It's been a great venue because of its size and it's so easy to get to, but I'm sure historical Frankston Hall will suit us just fine.

15
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Our social committee plans and organises club trips from time to time and they're always looking for suggestions from members for new places to go to.

16
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:39,000
If you join you should check the activities list that's posted on a website each month and attend anything that interests you.

17
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Come and make friends we're just one big happy family.

18
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:52,000
So how do you join and what about membership fees? It's simple. Just fill in the form and give it to me before you leave this morning.

19
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:02,000
There are a few payment options. Some members prefer to make an annual payment which is a slightly cheaper option or you can pay monthly.

20
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Why don't you get a group together it makes the activities more fun.

21
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Before you hear the rest of the talk you have some time to look at questions 16 to 20.

22
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Now listen and answer a question 16 to 20.

23
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:57,000
If you still haven't decided whether to join or not let me try to tempt you with some of our upcoming events.

24
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Our moonlight wildlife walk was previously available to members immediate families as well.

25
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:10,000
But this wonderful activities become so popular that it's now limited to just members.

26
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Although it's free we do ask our members to pay something to the wildlife fund so it can continue its good work.

27
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Everyone makes their way to the wildlife park independently arriving at dusk where a guide walks with the group and tells us about all the animals we encounter.

28
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Okay theater in the park we see a different play every month.

29
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:40,000
The parks on the train line and easy to access so we don't organise buses or anything.

30
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Come along and recline on a blanket on the grass although some members prefer to take along their own seat.

31
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
No need to make a reservation there's plenty of space.

32
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:59,000
After the play we all walk to a local cafe where you can purchase coffee and cake. It's a really fun night out.

33
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Birdwatching is a regular activity and it's organised by the keen bird watches in the club.

34
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:14,000
This activity consists mainly of early morning and late afternoon walking trips to spot the birds when they're most active.

35
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Birdwatching attracts only small numbers so one of our ardent birdwatches drives members in the club van to the best spots.

36
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:29,000
The City Botanical Gardens Walk is a popular activity that occurs a couple of times a year.

37
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Members make their own way there and usually meet up outside the gates at 8.45am setting off for the hours walk with the volunteer guide by 9am.

38
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Many members bring a friend or relative and this is fine.

39
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Now the state library our visits here in the past have always been great because there's something for everyone.

40
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
You can easily spend a whole day in there.

41
00:05:54,000 --> 00:06:03,000
There's a lovely restaurant and you can take food into the small cinema there where we'll be watching a short film about the history of our local area.

42
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:15,000
That is the end of part 2. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to part 2.

